+# VSeed S40 local implementation — review reference (Issue #41)
+
+Provided by @Od1n666 for review by @dimitrilendi-tech, @lientry, and @iamkaku.
+
+**IMPORTANT: This is a REFERENCE PATCH, not a drop-in functional upstream integration PR.**
+All files are added under `examples/vseed_s40_local_reference/`. Existing upstream source files are not modified or replaced. Developers can compare and selectively port the implementation to the maintained GrowHub architecture.
+
+## Scope
+- Local experimental S40-only integration snapshot, extracted from the user-provided ZIP (no `old/`, `__pycache__/`, or generated bytecode).
+- 14-day propagation package at `examples/vseed_steckling.yaml`.
+- Local snapshot includes S40 state, commands, entities and protocol support files; it is not guaranteed to match latest upstream.
+
+## Applying the patch
+```bash
+git checkout -b review/od1n666-vseed-s40-reference
+git apply --check vseed_s40_reference.patch
+git apply vseed_s40_reference.patch
+```
+
+The package uses `input_datetime.vseed_stecklinge_startdatum`, which must be configured separately when using the original package; the example is not plug-and-play without setup and an exposed set of matching S40 entities.
+
+## Safety
+No personal Home Assistant runtime config, login tokens, raw diagnostic dumps or local cache files are intentionally included. Review all source content before republishing. The code is untested against the current upstream runtime.
+
+## Requested further tests
+- `seed.state` phases 2/3
+- `lackWater` with filled tank, manual quick watering
+- `heaterLv` response to `tTemp`
